@startuml defense-composition
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam rectangleBorderThickness 2
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
skinparam nodesep 10
skinparam ranksep 20

title Defense Composition: No Single Layer Stops Everything

' Left side: defense layers as a stack
rectangle "**Content-Addressed Trust** (G1, G3)\nBlocks: zero-click MCP, TOCTOU" as TRUST #70a1ff
rectangle "**Input Sanitization** (G7)\nBlocks: invisible Unicode injection" as INPUT #a8e6cf
rectangle "**Phantom Proxy**\nBlocks: HTTP credential exfiltration" as PROXY #a8e6cf
rectangle "**SSRF Defense + Network Isolation** (G8)\nBlocks: DNS exfil, SSRF, metadata access" as SSRF #a8e6cf
rectangle "**WASM Capability Isolation**\nBlocks: shell hijack, env read, binary planting" as WASMBOX #00b894
rectangle "**OS Sandbox** (bwrap / gVisor / Seatbelt)\nBlocks: filesystem escape, network exfil via bash" as OS #ffd32a

' Stack them
OS -up-> SSRF : ""
SSRF -up-> PROXY : ""
PROXY -up-> INPUT : ""
INPUT -up-> TRUST : ""
WASMBOX -up[hidden]-> OS

' Right side: attacks
rectangle "Zero-click MCP autoload" as A1 #ff7675
rectangle "TOCTOU trust persistence" as A2 #ff7675
rectangle "Adversarial Unicode injection" as A3 #ff7675
rectangle "HTTP credential exfiltration" as A4 #ff7675
rectangle "DNS / SSRF exfiltration" as A5 #ff7675
rectangle "Shell hijack / binary planting" as A6 #ff7675
rectangle "Kernel exploit escape" as A7 #ff7675

' Attack → blocked-by arrows
A1 -left[#green,dashed]-> TRUST : blocked
A2 -left[#green,dashed]-> TRUST : blocked
A3 -left[#green,dashed]-> INPUT : blocked
A4 -left[#green,dashed]-> PROXY : blocked
A5 -left[#green,dashed]-> SSRF : blocked
A6 -left[#green,dashed]-> WASMBOX : blocked
A7 -left[#red,dashed]-> OS : <color:red>**NOT blocked**</color>\n<color:red>(needs gVisor/Firecracker)</color>

' Position WASM alongside OS
WASMBOX -right[hidden]-> A6

note bottom of OS
  **Key insight:** No single layer stops all 7 attacks.
  Layers compose — each blocks a different category.
  The kernel exploit gap requires hardware isolation (Firecracker).
end note

@enduml
